/applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIDAKA SHIGEYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUMAGAI KIYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHKAWARA ICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA TOMOO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIDAKA, SHIGEYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUMAGAI, KIYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHKAWARA, ICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, TOMOO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A bellows type pressure responding valve having a sealed bellows (66) as a pressure sensing element and adapted to change a valve opening by transmitting the expansion/contraction of the bellows (66) to a valve disc (61) via a valve stem (65) supported by a valve housing (51) movably in a valve lift direction, wherein a spherical joint structure consisting of a ball (77) disposed coaxially with the valve stem (65) and a spherical recess (78) formed at the bellows center position of a closing end face (67a) at the bellows body (67) of the bellows (66) is assembled into a connection between the bellows (66) and the stem (65) to spherically connect the bellows (66) with the stem (65) by the spherical joint structure, thereby delivering an automatic centripetal action between the bellows and the stem to provide high-accuracy valve control characteristics.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une soupape agissant en réponse à la pression du type à soufflet. Cette soupape comprend un soufflet (66) à fermeture étanche comme élément sensible à la pression et adapté pour modifier une ouverture de la soupape en transmettant la dilatation/contraction du soufflet (66) à un disque de soupape (61) via une tige de soupape (65) supportée par un logement de soupape (51) de manière mobile dans le sens de levée de la soupape. Une structure d'assemblage sphérique se composant d'une bille (77) disposée de manière coaxiale par rapport à la tige (65) de soupape et un évidement sphérique (78) ménagé au centre d'une face d'extrémité de fermeture (67a) du corps (67) du soufflet (66) est assemblé entre ce dernier (66) et la tige (65) pour relier de manière sphérique ledit soufflet (66) à ladite tige (65). Cela assure une action centripète automatique entre le soufflet et la tige et confère à la soupape des caractéristiques de commande de haute précision.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>